WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
- Where can I find a crib?

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.040
Crib, crib, crib, crib.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.260
Crib, crib, crib.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.110
Crib, crib, crib.

00:00:07.054 --> 00:00:08.350
- [Man] Do you just wanna explain

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.928
what's happening right now?

00:00:09.928 --> 00:00:12.928
(suspenseful music)

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.760
- I'm trying to think of
what object I want to use

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.390
as the experiment to see if
my phone is listening to me.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.530
I put my phone outside of the room.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.750
The object has to be so
specific, but so unrelated to me

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.020
that there is no possibly way

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.040
that this ad would be
suggested to me aside

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.210
from my phone listening
to me and giving me an ad.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.590
I can not type it on my
phone, can't search for it.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.360
I sound like such a psycho.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.896
Kid-related stuff, like a crib.

00:01:00.896 --> 00:01:03.060
- Oh.
- I'm never buying anything

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.060
for a kid.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.434
I haven't been looking and
I don't plan on looking

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.300
for something like that.
- That's a really good idea.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.871
I like that a lot.

00:01:08.871 --> 00:01:09.704
- Is it crib?

00:01:09.704 --> 00:01:10.537
- [Man] I think it's crib.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:11.370
- Is it crib?

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.203
All right.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.650
So because this is science
and we wanna make this

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.410
a fair experiment, I'm
going to set some parameters

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.750
for myself about how this is conducted.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.950
For the next week, every day I'm going

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.290
to say the crib 50 times.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.480
I think that's gonna be
a fair assessment to see

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.030
if my phone is listening to me.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.470
Crib, crib, crib.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.640
Does anyone where I can buy a baby's crib?

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.130
Taking a walk, gonna go
meet my wife for lunch,

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.200
and I figured I'd squeeze
a couple cribs in.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.370
Crib, crib, crib, crib, crib.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.200
Just eating some pizza, crib, crib.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.080
Where do you think I'd buy a crib?

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.730
I keep getting excited
because this will be so crazy

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.910
if I'm on my phone one day
and I see an ad for a crib.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.950
I wonder if my phone's listening to me.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.690
Does anyone where I can get a crib?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.180
I'm gonna be honest,
it feels a little weird

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.560
to sit in my apartment
just saying the word crib

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.290
over and over again.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.260
I hope my neighbors aren't listening.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.093
I'm about to go to sleep,

00:02:16.093 --> 00:02:18.570
but I thought I should get some cribs in.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.440
Crib, crib, crib, can you hear me, iPhone?

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.010
It's day two, just left the gym.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.310
It's a disgusting
morning here in New York.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.710
Perfect time to squeeze in some cribs.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.630
Can anyone hear me?

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.570
I'd like to buy a baby's crib.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:32.720
Of all the words I could've picked

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.260
to be saying over and over
again, crib is a weird one.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.450
Crib, crib, crib, crib.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.146
Chelsea, do you know where I'd
be able to buy a baby's crib?

00:02:41.146 --> 00:02:42.670
- What are you gonna use that crib for?

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.240
- How do you pronounce it?

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.253
Crib?

00:02:45.253 --> 00:02:46.086
- Crib.

00:02:46.086 --> 00:02:46.920
- Crib, okay.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.410
Crib, crib.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.930
Baby's crib, crib for a baby.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:55.780
Crib.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:01.720
Grinding at the gym, crib, crib, crib.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.650
I don't know, I'm losing
faith in this experiment.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.930
I think I'm actually getting scared

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.450
that I'm gonna be on Facebook
or Instagram or Twitter

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.100
and there is gonna be a crib advertisement

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.440
and I'm just gonna miss it completely.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.840
And then it's all gonna be for nothing.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.673
I don't know guys.

00:03:15.673 --> 00:03:18.340
I've just been cribbing
away all day every day.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.730
I've been really trying to pay attention

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.920
to the ads that are on my social media

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.870
and so far I've only seen
Dick's Sporting Goods,

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.720
there was a movie advertisement,
Glade the air freshener,

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.600
a grocery delivery
service, and Volkswagon.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.930
None of which are crib based.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.100
Not even remotely baby oriented.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.480
My ability to say crib
into my phone 50 times

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.690
while it's not going
anything is dwindling.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.410
None the less, I really wanna see this out

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.810
through the end of the
week because science.

00:03:49.337 --> 00:03:54.337
Crib, crib, crib, crib,
crib, crib, crib, crib.

00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:00.592
It's the end of the week.

00:04:00.592 --> 00:04:02.310
It's the last day of the experiment.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:05.530
I'm starting to think this was
a gigantic waste of my time.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:08.690
I haven't seen anything on
any social media platform

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.980
that is a suggested ad for cribs.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.060
I thought somebody was listening to me.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.470
If you're still listening to me,

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.609
you're making me look like an idiot.

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:21.609
Crib, crib, crib, crib. (laughs)

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.460
They're not listening to me.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.550
You have no idea how badly
I wanted to make this work

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:31.570
just by typing a little
crib into my phone.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.710
Just to see if something would happen,

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.860
but this is an experiment

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.610
and I wouldn't do that to you guys.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.080
Okay, so it's day whatever,
I don't know what day it is

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.740
in this experiment,
but I've had a thought.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.810
Whoever listening to me
in my phone is dead set

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.800
on making me look like an absolute moron.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.320
So I think I'm gonna
try some other tactics

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.110
to get crib as a suggested
ad in my social media.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.320
Some of a bitch, it's my phone now.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.130
Someone texted me crib.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.310
Word must've gotten out about
this experiment I'm doing.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.110
So I don't know, maybe this'll help.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.050
All right, here's the deal.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.490
Maybe my phone is listening
to me, maybe it isn't.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.323
I don't know.

00:05:06.323 --> 00:05:07.540
I haven't seen any evidence of it.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.310
So I put a little search into Google Maps.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.850
Not looking for a crib,
but for a Babies R Us.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.070
They've got cribs.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:15.120
So I don't know if my phone
gonna track me to this store

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.500
and then suggest something for me,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.360
but I've got some shopping to do.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.480
Little did I know, I'm on the wrong floor.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.690
I've gotta go to level
three for the cribs.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.170
Something weird is going on.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.310
I get up here.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.250
Half the room is empty.

00:05:41.768 --> 00:05:42.800
I gotta get the fuck out of here.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.410
So I just left Babies R Us

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.280
and I'm not sure whether I should laugh

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.570
or chuckle or freak out.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.280
There was not a single
crib in the entire place.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.610
Literally everything but cribs.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.040
I know my phone is listening to me.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:55.880
Guy, you gotta believe me.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.920
My phone is listening to me,
crib, crib, crib, crib, crib.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.410
I've actually thought about
why it's not coming up

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.250
on my phone and I don't think

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.890
I've been saying crib loud enough.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.240
Crib, crib, crib!

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.720
Get me a god damn crib.

00:06:09.052 --> 00:06:09.990
(sighs) Fuck.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.985
Do you think I'm proud of
the way I've been acting?

00:06:14.985 --> 00:06:16.180
I shouldn't be, it's embarrassing.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.430
Now the time has come
to do the unthinkable.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.350
So now it's your move, iPhone.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.130
Listen up everybody, this is
the last day of the experiment.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.330
I can't do this anymore.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.580
If I get to the office and
there's not a suggested ad

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.700
for cribs in my social media, we're done.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.533
We're done.

00:06:38.533 --> 00:06:40.170
That's it, guys.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.160
It's the end of well over two
weeks of just rambling crib

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.210
into my phone.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.980
Went through my suggested ads again.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.810
It's Coca-Cola, it's
Ziploc, Dannon Yogurt.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.080
I really thought this was going to work.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.430
I wanted it to work.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.410
The more I think about
it though in reality,

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.000
it's probably a good
thing this didn't work.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.510
So in general, does it mean your phone is

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.300
or isn't listening to you?

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.430
I still don't know.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:05.760
That's not for me to say.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.600
In terms of cribs, no it
is not listening to me.

